  "notes": "Heating load only in the winter months (Nov-Apr), heaviest Dec-Feb; May is left at zero as mild. Two daily peaks — a morning warm-up around 7-8am and a larger evening one around 7-8pm, the latter overlapping the on-peak window. Only the distribution is used; scale it by an annual kWh you supply. Default 2500 kWh/yr suits a heat pump or moderate electric heating — resistance heat would be much higher."
